s9-2-p13 = prose (cons "Here \(\nu^{\!*}\) denotes finite iteration or guarded continuation of the *labeled* machine/evaluator simulation, and the semicolon is composition of evidence, not equality of machine states. The machine-simulation premise includes progress for each admitted evaluator transition (or an explicit related fault/resource outcome), together with matching divergence and fairness conditions whenever the selected observation distinguishes them. Under those premises, the realization does not merely exclude incorrect target observations; it can actually follow each admitted evaluator run through the corresponding finite or guarded target behavior. An executable image may be common to all \(c\); the encoded initial configuration varies. The statement is relative to the target machine and world model, including resource and loader conditions. An emitted command with no supplied response remains an explicit world obligation; the machine simulation cannot silently discharge it. " nil)
